S9: no file names, texts, PINs or peer data in the logs

Upstream logs what the user and the peer send, several times at info
level: every file name offered and the path it will be written to, the
whole consent metadata (names, text previews, the sender's name), the
created file, the handshake PIN, the RemoteDeviceInfo, the paths the
sender opens and the SendInfo the application sends (paths again), every
chunk's file name and folder, each resolved mDNS service with the peer's
name, and any unhandled encrypted frame in full, whatever it carries. The
peer's own strings end up in the log verbatim (the UKEY2 next-protocol
string, for one), which lets a peer write into it. Per-chunk progress is
logged at info level, one line per chunk.

Sukkula's rule (spec S9): logging is off by default, and never includes
file names or text at info level; secrets are never logged. Here the log
lines keep what helps with a protocol problem (states, frame types,
payload ids, sizes, device types, addresses at debug) and drop names,
paths, texts, the PIN and peer-chosen strings; per-chunk lines move to
trace.

Findings: S9. Report: docs/UPSTREAM-QUICKSHARE.md R13.
